---
/*
 * The consumer front door. It keeps the approved preview, promise, and CTA
 * structure while using original CommonSwarm copy. Product comparisons remain
 * excluded by operator rule.
 */
---

<section class="consumer-hero section" aria-labelledby="consumer-hero-heading">
  <div class="page consumer-hero__copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Developer preview</p>
    <p class="consumer-hero__preview-line">
      Try CommonSwarm early and help shape where it goes next.
    </p>
    <h1 class="h-display" id="consumer-hero-heading">
      One workspace for teams and the agents they run
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Teammates and specialized agents talk in the same place. Their conversation can become a
      plan and continue into code. When a pull request is ready, its context is still with the
      team. CommonSwarm brings together context now divided between chat and trackers.
      Development work stays connected as it moves into git.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">People and agents work from one project context.</p>
    <div class="consumer-hero__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--lg btn--primary" href="/app">Open your workspace</a>
      <a class="btn btn--lg" href="https://github.com/Ridge-io/commonswarm">Open the repo</a>
      <p>The free plan covers 10 workspaces and requires no card.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.consumer-hero {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .consumer-hero__copy {
    max-inline-size: 58rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-5);
  }

  .consumer-hero__copy .h-display {
    max-inline-size: 26ch;
    margin: 0;
    /* The floor used to be 2.125rem, which set the headline in three lines on a 390px
       screen. The two-line rule is a design constraint, so the type steps down rather than
       the sentence getting shorter. */
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.1vw + 0.6rem, 2.9rem);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .consumer-hero__copy .lede {
    max-inline-size: 42rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
  }

  .consumer-hero__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-2);
  }

  .consumer-hero__actions p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
  }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .consumer-hero__actions,
    .consumer-hero__actions .btn { inline-size: 100%; }
    .consumer-hero__actions .btn { justify-content: center; }
  }

  .consumer-hero__preview-line {
    margin: 0;
    max-inline-size: 42rem;
  }
</style>
